+// gateup_exact.hpp -- exact int8 expansion + grouped MMAC GEMM for the gate/up product.
+//
+// Formats covered: IQ3_XXS (98 B/block), IQ2_S (82), IQ3_S (110), IQ4_XS (136) -- i.e. all 48
+// gate/up layers of this model. Opt-in, default off (STRATA_MMQ_GATEUP_EXACT=1).
+//
+// The original quantized weights stay canonical: every code and every FP32 scale written by these
+// expanders is bit-exact against ggml's own to_float for the same bytes (verified on real expert
+// blobs for all four formats). The GEMM then reads the same Q8 D4 activations the production MMQ
+// path reads, so only the *weight* representation changes.
+//
+// Weight scale granularity: IQ2_S needs one scale per 16 k-values (two per 32); the other three
+// formats need one per 32. The 32-deep int8 MMA cannot express two scales inside its own k-window,
+// so for IQ2_S the k-window is split by zeroing the A fragment in the lanes that hold the wrong
+// half (lane k-coverage is lg*8..lg*8+7), giving two exact 16-deep dots per MMAC pair. No extra
+// LDS staging is needed for that split.
